  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C4.S2 — CHSH: local bound, quantum value, Tsirelson</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C4.S2 — Bell and Tsirelson bounds</p></div><p>(a) Give the maximum of \(|S|\) over all local hidden-variable models.</p><p>\(S_{\mathrm{LHV}}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the exact maximum of \(|S|\) allowed by quantum mechanics (the Tsirelson bound), as an exact expression.</p><p>\(S_{Q}=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) On \(|\Phi^{+}\rangle\) with \(A_0=Z\), \(A_1=X\) and Bob measuring \(\cos\beta\,Z+\sin\beta\,X\), the correlator \(\langle A_0 B\rangle\) equals a simple function of \(\beta\). Give it.</p><p>\(\langle A_0B\rangle=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) In a deterministic local model \(A_0(B_0+B_1)+A_1(B_0-B_1)=\pm2\) pointwise, and general local models are convex mixtures, so \(|S|\le2\).</p><p>(b) Tsirelson: \(|S|\le2\sqrt2\), attained with the settings of §3. The gap between \(2\) and \(2\sqrt2\) is the experimentally certified non-locality; no-signalling alone would allow \(4\).</p><p>(c) On \(|\Phi^{+}\rangle\), \(\langle Z\otimes Z\rangle=1\) and \(\langle Z\otimes X\rangle=0\), so \(\langle A_0B\rangle=\cos\beta\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
